   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the assessor of the town of Islip to accept an application for exemption from real property taxes from the Gospel Tabernacle Church of God in Christ for certain parcels of land located in the town of Islip",
    "basePrintNo": "S2598",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2598-2013",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S2598\n\nTITLE  OF BILL:  An act authorizing the assessor of the town of Islip to\naccept an application for exemption from real property  taxes  from  the\nGospel  Tabernacle  Church  of God in Christ for certain parcels of land\nlocated in the town of Islip\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:   To grant the town  assessor  for  the\ntown  of  Islip  the authority to exempt the Gospel Tabernacle Church of\nGod in Christ (also known as the \"Common Ground Church\"), a not-fox-pro-\nfit church, from liability for payment of real property taxes  on  their\nparsonage  property  that  was due on the assessment rolls for 2009-2010\nand 2010-2011, 2011-2012.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection One authorizes and directs the assessor of the town of Islip  to\naccept  an  application from the Common Ground Church for exemption from\nreal property taxes pursuant to Section 420-a of the real  property  tax\nlaw  for  the  assessment  rolls  of  years  2009-2012 for the parsonage\nlocated on property in Central Islip. Upon satisfaction that the  Common\nGround  Church would have otherwise been entitled to said exemption, the\nassessor may grant this  exemption  from  all  taxation  beginning  with\nrespect  to  these  rolls.  If  exemption  is granted, the church may be\nrefunded any taxes paid and any taxes, fines, penalties, liens or inter-\nest unpaid may be cancelled through the  sole  discretion  of  the  town\nboard.\n\nSection Two is the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:  The parsonage property associated with the Common Ground\nChurch is expected to receive tax-exempt status in 2012. This bill would\nauthorize  the  assessor of the town of Islip to accept application from\nthe Common Ground Church for exemption from real property taxes paid  on\nthe parsonage pursuant to Section 420-a of the real property tax law for\nassessment  rolls  from 2008-2011 which would refund to the church their\ntaxes for the years before this property was given tax exempt status.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: S.4722-B (of 2012).\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None to the State.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:  This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
